# WebAudits Performance & Core Web Vitals Optimization

When auditing or optimizing frontend performance, Largest Contentful Paint (LCP), or DOM tree depth, follow these rules:

## 1. Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) Subparts
- Break LCP into: TTFB, Resource Load Delay, Resource Load Duration, and Element Render Delay.
- Never add `loading="lazy"` to above-the-fold or hero images (spikes Load Delay by 1.5s+).
- Use `<link rel="preload" as="image" href="..." fetchpriority="high">` in `<head>`.
- Add `decoding="async"` to non-blocking images.

## 2. DOM Bloat & INP Prevention
- Maintain total DOM elements under 1,500 nodes and maximum tree depth under 32 levels.
- Eliminate redundant wrapper `<div>` elements ("div soup").
- Virtualize long lists exceeding 50 items.

## 3. Remote Audit Integration
- Audit any live URL using the WebAudits MCP server (`https://webaudits.pro/api/mcp`) or web inspector at https://webaudits.pro.
